{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CdJRdMDUL3MFLnQdkUeSH5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd035-rmdir\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/rmdir: Remove Empty Directories\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Cleanup scripts and build systems remove empty directories after deleting their contents.\n6\t  The macOS BSD rmdir lacks the --ignore-fail-on-non-empty and --verbose flags present in\n7\t  GNU rmdir. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (grmdir,\n8\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations and edge cases, verified\n9\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Remove one or more empty directories specified as command-line arguments.\n13\t  - G2: Support recursive removal of empty ancestor directories with -p.\n14\t  - G3: Support suppression of specific error conditions with --ignore-fail-on-non-empty.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Basic empty directory removal\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must remove a single empty directory when invoked as 'rmdir DIR'.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: Must remove multiple empty directories when invoked with multiple DIR arguments, processing each independently.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when a target directory is not empty.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when a target does not exist or is not a directory.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Parent removal (-p, --parents)\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: -p or --parents must remove the target directory and then remove each successive empty parent component of the path, similar to 'rmdir -p a/b/c' removing c, then b, then a.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must stop ascending when a parent directory is not empty and report an error for that component.\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: Must process each DIR argument independently when -p is combined with multiple arguments.\n38\t\n39\t  R3:\n40\t    title: Error handling and verbosity\n41\t    items:\n42\t      - R3.1:\n43\t          text: --ignore-fail-on-non-empty must suppress error messages and the non-zero exit status caused by a directory not being empty.\n44\t      - R3.2:\n45\t          text: --ignore-fail-on-non-empty must not suppress errors for other failure reasons such as permission denied or non-existent target.\n46\t      - R3.3:\n47\t          text: -v or --verbose must print a message to stdout for each directory successfully removed.\n48\t      - R3.4:\n49\t          text: Must exit 0 when all requested directories are successfully removed, and exit non-zero when any removal fails (unless suppressed by --ignore-fail-on-non-empty).\n50\t\n51\t  R4:\n52\t    title: Differential testing\n53\t    items:\n54\t      - R4.1:\n55\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and grmdir via pkg/testutils.\n56\t      - R4.2:\n57\t          text: \"Tests must cover: single empty directory removal, multiple directories, -p with nested empty directories, non-empty directory error, non-existent directory error, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty suppression, and -v verbose output.\"\n58\t      - R4.3:\n59\t          text: Tests must verify that -p stops ascending correctly when a parent is not empty, matching grmdir behavior.\n60\t\n61\tnon_goals:\n62\t  - cmd/rmdir does not remove non-empty directories; that is the role of rm -r.\n63\t  - cmd/rmdir does not accept file arguments; only directories are valid targets.\n64\t  - cmd/rmdir does not read directory names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n65\t\n66\tacceptance_criteria:\n67\t  - id: AC1\n68\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir emptydir removes an empty directory, matching grmdir.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R1.1\n71\t      - R1.2\n72\t      - R1.3\n73\t      - R2.1\n74\t      - R2.2\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t      - R3.2\n77\t      - R3.4\n78\t      - R4.2\n79\t      - R4.3\n80\t  - id: AC2\n81\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir -p a/b/c removes c, b, and a when all are empty, matching grmdir -p.\"\n82\t    traces:\n83\t      - R1.1\n84\t      - R1.2\n85\t      - R1.3\n86\t      - R2.1\n87\t      - R2.2\n88\t      - R2.3\n89\t      - R3.1\n90\t      - R3.2\n91\t      - R3.4\n92\t      - R4.2\n93\t      - R4.3\n94\t  - id: AC3\n95\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir nonempty exits non-zero with an error message when nonempty contains files, matching grmdir.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R1.1\n98\t      - R1.2\n99\t      - R1.3\n100\t      - R1.4\n101\t      - R2.1\n102\t      - R2.2\n103\t      - R3.1\n104\t      - R3.2\n105\t      - R3.4\n106\t      - R4.1\n107\t      - R4.2\n108\t      - R4.3\n109\t  - id: AC4\n110\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir --ignore-fail-on-non-empty nonempty exits 0 silently, matching grmdir.\"\n111\t    traces:\n112\t      - R1.1\n113\t      - R1.2\n114\t      - R1.3\n115\t      - R1.4\n116\t      - R2.1\n117\t      - R2.2\n118\t      - R3.1\n119\t      - R3.2\n120\t      - R3.4\n121\t      - R4.1\n122\t      - R4.2\n123\t      - R4.3\n124\t  - id: AC5\n125\t    criterion: \"Differential test against grmdir passes for empty removal, -p, non-empty errors, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty, and -v.\"\n126\t    traces:\n127\t      - R1.1\n128\t      - R1.2\n129\t      - R1.3\n130\t      - R1.4\n131\t      - R2.1\n132\t      - R2.2\n133\t      - R2.3\n134\t      - R3.1\n135\t      - R3.2\n136\t      - R3.3\n137\t      - R3.4\n138\t      - R4.1\n139\t      - R4.2\n140\t      - R4.3\n141\t  - id: AC6\n142\t    criterion: \"cmd/rmdir compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n143\t    traces:\n144\t      - R1.1\n145\t      - R1.2\n146\t      - R1.3\n147\t      - R1.4\n148\t      - R2.1\n149\t      - R2.2\n150\t      - R2.3\n151\t      - R3.1\n152\t      - R3.2\n153\t      - R3.3\n154\t      - R3.4\n155\t      - R4.1\n156\t      - R4.2\n157\t      - R4.3\n158\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27e152ad-d1f1-4cc7-a457-db1756e18797","uuid":"7ef62548-5f77-454b-8486-5fb9a7ece2cf","timestamp":"2026-05-20T10:51:53.639Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5332/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd035-rmdir.yaml","content":"id: srd035-rmdir\ntitle: \"cmd/rmdir: Remove Empty Directories\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Cleanup scripts and build systems remove empty directories after deleting their contents.\n  The macOS BSD rmdir lacks the --ignore-fail-on-non-empty and --verbose flags present in\n  GNU rmdir. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (grmdir,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations and edge cases, verified\n  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Remove one or more empty directories specified as command-line arguments.\n  - G2: Support recursive removal of empty ancestor directories with -p.\n  - G3: Support suppression of specific error conditions with --ignore-fail-on-non-empty.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic empty directory removal\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must remove a single empty directory when invoked as 'rmdir DIR'.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must remove multiple empty directories when invoked with multiple DIR arguments, processing each independently.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when a target directory is not empty.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when a target does not exist or is not a directory.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Parent removal (-p, --parents)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -p or --parents must remove the target directory and then remove each successive empty parent component of the path, similar to 'rmdir -p a/b/c' removing c, then b, then a.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must stop ascending when a parent directory is not empty and report an error for that component.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must process each DIR argument independently when -p is combined with multiple arguments.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Error handling and verbosity\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: --ignore-fail-on-non-empty must suppress error messages and the non-zero exit status caused by a directory not being empty.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: --ignore-fail-on-non-empty must not suppress errors for other failure reasons such as permission denied or non-existent target.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: -v or --verbose must print a message to stdout for each directory successfully removed.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all requested directories are successfully removed, and exit non-zero when any removal fails (unless suppressed by --ignore-fail-on-non-empty).\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and grmdir via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: single empty directory removal, multiple directories, -p with nested empty directories, non-empty directory error, non-existent directory error, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty suppression, and -v verbose output.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that -p stops ascending correctly when a parent is not empty, matching grmdir behavior.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/rmdir does not remove non-empty directories; that is the role of rm -r.\n  - cmd/rmdir does not accept file arguments; only directories are valid targets.\n  - cmd/rmdir does not read directory names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir emptydir removes an empty directory, matching grmdir.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir -p a/b/c removes c, b, and a when all are empty, matching grmdir -p.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir nonempty exits non-zero with an error message when nonempty contains files, matching grmdir.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rmdir --ignore-fail-on-non-empty nonempty exits 0 silently, matching grmdir.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against grmdir passes for empty removal, -p, non-empty errors, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty, and -v.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/rmdir compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":158,"startLine":1,"totalLines":158}}}
