{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing stitch task #5332 for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd035-rmdir requirements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, and R3.4 — specifically \"Error handling and verbosity\" features for the `cmd/rmdir` utility. The existing implementation already covers R1.1-R1.4 (basic removal) and R2.1-R2.3 (parent removal with `-p`). The task requires modifying `cmd/rmdir/main.go` and `cmd/rmdir/rmdir_test.go` to add:\n   - R3.1: `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty` suppresses error messages and non-zero exit for non-empty directories\n   - R3.2: `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty` must NOT suppress other error types (permission denied, non-existent)\n   - R3.3: `-v`/`--verbose` prints a message to stdout for each successfully removed directory\n   - R3.4: Exit 0 on full success, non-zero on failure (unless suppressed by `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty`)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`grmdir`)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary` for test infrastructure\n   - `syscall.Rmdir` for directory removal at the syscall level\n   - `syscall.Errno` type assertions for distinguishing error types (ENOTEMPTY vs ENOENT vs EACCES etc.)\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at start of main\n   - GNU rmdir verbose format: `rmdir: removing directory, 'PATH'`\n   - Flag parsing is manual (no cobra) — custom `parseArgs`, `parseLongFlag`, `parseShortFlags`\n   - The `options` struct already has all three boolean fields defined but `verbose` and `ignoreFailOnNonEmpty` are not yet used in the `run()` function\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd035-rmdir.yaml`\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1-R4 and acceptance criteria\n     - R3.1: `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty must suppress error messages and the non-zero exit status caused by a directory not being empty.`\n     - R3.2: `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty must not suppress errors for other failure reasons such as permission denied or non-existent target.`\n     - R3.3: `-v or --verbose must print a message to stdout for each directory successfully removed.`\n     - R3.4: `Must exit 0 when all requested directories are successfully removed, and exit non-zero when any removal fails (unless suppressed by --ignore-fail-on-non-empty).`\n\n   - `cmd/rmdir/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3\n     - `options` struct has `parents`, `verbose`, `ignoreFailOnNonEmpty` fields\n     - Flag parsing already handles all flags including `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty`, `-v`, `--verbose`\n     - The `run()` function (lines 52-73) does NOT use `opts.verbose` or `opts.ignoreFailOnNonEmpty`\n     - Key code that needs modification — the `run()` function:\n     ```go\n     func run(opts options, dirs []string) int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, dir := range dirs {\n             if err := syscall.Rmdir(dir); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rmdir: failed to remove '%s': %s\\n\",\n                     dir, sysErrMsg(err))\n                 exitCode = 1\n                 continue\n             }\n             if opts.parents {\n                 for parent := filepath.Dir(filepath.Clean(dir)); parent != \".\" && parent != \"/\"; parent = filepath.Dir(parent) {\n                     if err := syscall.Rmdir(parent); err != nil {\n                         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rmdir: failed to remove directory '%s': %s\\n\",\n                             parent, sysErrMsg(err))\n                         exitCode = 1\n                         break\n                     }\n                 }\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     ```\n     - `sysErrMsg()` helper (lines 75-92) maps syscall.Errno to human-readable strings\n\n   - `cmd/rmdir/rmdir_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already has differential tests for: no args, nonexistent, not a directory, nonempty, single empty, multiple empty, partial failure, multiple nonexistent, parents nested empty, parents stop at nonempty, parents multiple args, parents single dir, parents nonexistent\n     - Uses both `testutils.RunDiffTests` for simple cases and custom `runBin`/`compareResults` helpers for cases needing separate filesystem setup\n     - `normalizeBinaryName` replaces binary name paths in output for comparison\n     - Missing tests: `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty` (R3.1, R3.2), `-v` verbose output (R3.3), combined flags\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reads were performed before the summary request.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the `run()` function needs to:\n     1. Check if error is `syscall.ENOTEMPTY` when `ignoreFailOnNonEmpty` is true, and if so, skip error output and don't set exitCode=1\n     2. For non-ENOTEMPTY errors, always report them regardless of `ignoreFailOnNonEmpty`\n     3. Print verbose messages (`rmdir: removing directory, 'DIR'`) to stdout after successful removal\n     4. Apply the same logic during parent traversal (`-p`)\n   - Need a helper function like `isNonEmptyError(err error) bool` to check for ENOTEMPTY\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial massive task description providing: role, repository files, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task details, constraints, description, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a conversation summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/rmdir/main.go` to implement R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3