{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VyXd1UB6FbgkMJNvUgwbHN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! GNU rmdir with `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty` still prints a verbose message for the non-empty directory even though it's not actually removed. So when `--ignore-fail-on-non-empty` is set, GNU rmdir still prints verbose output for non-empty directories that it \"attempts\" to remove, even though the removal fails.\n\nWait, let me re-read the output:\n- ref stdout: `\"rmdir: removing directory, 'emptydir'\\nrmdir: removing directory, 'nonempty'\\n\"`\n\n\n- go stdout: `\"rmdir: removing directory, 'emptydir'\\n\"`\n\nSo the Go implementation isn't printing the verbose message for the non-empty directory at all, whereas GNU rmdir does. That's the discrepancy—GNU rmdir prints the message before attempting removal, so it shows up even when the directory can't be removed, but the Go version only prints it for successful removals.\n\nI need to adjust the code so that the verbose message gets printed regardless of whether the removal succeeds, matching GNU's behavior.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1330,"cache_read_input_tokens":32852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1330},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27e152ad-d1f1-4cc7-a457-db1756e18797","uuid":"6ca4cc8c-3288-452f-988e-5e7e59983798"}
